---
description: Rules for the Tauri desktop agent (Rust core and UI)
globs: apps/agent/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- READ-ONLY (ADR 010): capture the game window only (windows-capture cascade), Windows OCR, OS signals (sysinfo).
  Never: process memory, injection, DirectX hooks, packet capture, input that confirms in-game actions, server commands.
- Sensors implement the `Sensor` trait (id, active_in, interval, sample) and emit `Signal`s; fusion produces observations.
- Types from the generated JSON Schema (typify). Send `X-Agent-Version`; on 426 force the updater.
- `clippy -D warnings`, `rustfmt`, `cargo nextest`, `insta` snapshots for OCR fixtures, `cargo-mutants` on the core.
- Mutation proofs are unit tests only (ADR 026): `cargo nextest run -p d2rmm-agent-core --lib`, never `--workspace`,
  `--test` or the `tests/` directory. Logic that only the assembled loops can observe goes into a pure function in `src/`.
- CPU < 2% average (NFR-02); adaptive intervals per PC state.

## Layers and crates (ADR 027)

The agent is hexagonal, like the backend's Agents module. Three layers, one direction of dependency:
`adapters → application → domain`. Nothing in a lower layer points up. The Cargo crate boundaries enforce it.

| Layer       | Crate                        | Holds                                                                                                                       | May depend on                                                                                  | Must not depend on                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| ----------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| domain      | `d2rmm-agent-domain`         | aggregates, value objects, domain services, timing constants, pure rules and their errors                                  | `std`, `thiserror`, `chrono` and `uuid` (default features off)                                 | `tokio`, `reqwest`, `tauri`, `keyring`, `windows`, `serde`, `tracing`, `zeroize`, the generated contracts (`contracts::generated`), `d2rmm-agent-core`, `d2rmm-agent-adapters`, `d2rmm-agent`; any type named `Agent`          |
| application | `d2rmm-agent-core`           | ports (traits), use cases (pair, beat, follow the stream, post an observation, check for an update, read a frame), loops, `Runtime`, the view model, `Secret`, the loop spans | `d2rmm-agent-domain`                                                                 | `reqwest`, `tauri`, `keyring`, `windows`, the generated contracts, `d2rmm-agent-adapters`, `d2rmm-agent`                                                                                                                    |
| adapters    | `d2rmm-agent-adapters`       | the HTTP gateway, the generated contracts, the translation (ACL), the SSE parser and its limits, the client builder, telemetry bootstrap | `d2rmm-agent-core` (its ports), `d2rmm-agent-domain`, `reqwest`, `serde`, the generated contracts | `tauri`, `keyring`, `windows`, `d2rmm-agent`                                                                                                                                                                              |
| root        | `d2rmm-agent` (app crate)    | the composition root and the Windows and Tauri adapters: Credential Manager, toolhelp, Windows OCR, updater, window, system clock and ids | every layer below                                                                    | `Probe` or `start_with_probe` (the test probe stays out of the shipped binary)                                                                                                                                              |

- The composition root builds the adapters and hands them to the application as port groups. It holds no rule.
- **The domain reads no clock and no randomness.** Time and identifiers come in as arguments (`WallClock`, `IdGenerator`
  are ports, applied by the application). The domain clippy file bans `Instant::now`, `SystemTime::now`, `Utc::now`,
  `Local::now` and `Uuid::new_v4`, and it bans `std::env` reads.
- The domain names nothing `Agent`: the device's aggregate is `PairedDevice`, never mistaken for the backend's `Agent`.
- The domain emits no spans. Telemetry spans live in the application layer.
- Domain and application rules are proved by unit tests (`cargo nextest run -p d2rmm-agent-domain --lib`, and the same
  for `d2rmm-agent-core`), with in-memory fakes for the ports. No mocking crate in core.
